# SQL's `NOT IN`: DS0105 with a fix to `!in`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where customerId NOT IN ('a', 'b')
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..50
  PIPELINE@0..49
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..49
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      IN_EXPR@21..49
        NAME_REF@21..31
          IDENT@21..31 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
        IDENT@32..35 "NOT"
        WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
        IDENT@36..38 "IN"
        WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
        ARG_LIST@39..49
          L_PAREN@39..40 "("
          LITERAL@40..43
            STRING@40..43 "'a'"
          COMMA@43..44 ","
          WHITESPACE@44..45 " "
          LITERAL@45..48
            STRING@45..48 "'b'"
          R_PAREN@48..49 ")"
  WHITESPACE@49..50 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `NOT IN` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:33
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where customerId NOT IN ('a', 'b')
  |                                 ^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: write `!in` to test that a value is not in a list

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where customerId !in ('a', 'b')
which parses without errors
